    "description": {
      "value": "<div data-ft-phase5-vocab-scrub=\"v1\" style=\"display:none\"></div>\n<p><strong>Living Relic Artificer.</strong> You specialize in crafting items that remember the people they were made for.</p><ul><li>During a Soma Break, you can designate one non-consumable item (weapon, armor, tool, or holy symbol) as a <strong>Living Relic</strong> for one creature.</li><li>While attuned to or carrying that item, the creature gains a small, persistent benefit of your choosing, such as +1 to a specific skill check, +1 to defense checks against fear, or +1 to one type of tool check (GM approval required).</li><li>You can maintain a number of Living Relics at a time equal to your tier. Creating a new one beyond that limit causes the oldest to lose its blessing.</li></ul><p>This feat provides narrative permission and a light mechanical framework for Soul-Smith “living relic” gear. The exact bonus is agreed upon with the GM when each relic is made.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
